# almost-open authoring

Standing repo law: [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). Keep agent policy out of generated site pages and lesson chrome.

## Open course

- Public curriculum lives only under `course/`. Anyone may read everything there.
- Do **not** reintroduce `student/`, `instructor/`, facilitator-only paths, or audience gates.

## Pedagogy

- Spine is **weeks 1–15** (HTMAA course-design). Each week page is the required practice path.
- Template: **Time**, **Goal**, **Steps**, **Done when**. No honesty banners on week pages.
- Provenance and source pointers go in `course/references.md` only.
- Do not invent lecture transcripts where evidence is missing. Gaps stay gaps.
- Prefer FOSS worked paths. Commercial tools are catalog alternatives, not mandates.
- Lab safety training and local machine settings override any number in a guide.
- Assessment signals (Done when) stay even when depth is thin.

## Site

- Eleventy builds from `course/**/*.md` only. Shallow URLs: `/`, `/weeks/`, `/weeks/NN/`, `/references/` (served under pathPrefix `/almost-open/` on project Pages).
- Keep the reading-first light theme; do not re-port a1-workshop.github.io proposal chrome as the course UI.
- Curriculum edits stay in this repo (`course/`, `site/`). Org hub listing lives in sibling `a1-workshop.github.io` — link the live hub URL from README/references when needed; do not vendor `course/` into the hub.

## Adding a week

1. Add or edit `course/weeks/NN-slug.md`.
2. Link it from `course/index.md` week table.
3. Add process/tool notes under `course/processes/` or `course/tools/` only when the week needs them.
